[Music]  okay so this is my review  of the new hbo max film which was  acquired from sony pictures  an american pickle this is based off of  a short story  written by simon rich in 2013  called sellout he also wrote the  teleplay here this was directed by  brandon troust this is his first  film he's directing solo he is known for  being the cinematographer on  most of seth rogen's projects film stars  seth rogen  in both lead roles here as herschel  greenbaum and ben greenbaum also in the  film are  sarah snook from succession fame and  yorma tocconi from lonely island  now if you come to watch this movie  because of sarah snook or yorman takoni  you're in the wrong place  i think sarah snook has about five  minutes in the beginning of this film  and yorma is in about three minutes a  little bit of the false advertising by  hbo max it was smart because they want  to get  sarah snook fans in there from  succession but she  is barely a player in this film she's in  the intro and that's about it  this movie is full on seth rogen if you  are not a seth rogen die hard  i don't know what to tell you here so  the story really is hershel green bomb  this jewish immigrant worker in 1920 he  falls into a vat of pickles and he wakes  up a hundred years later the same age  his body totally preserved and he looks  for family he's in brooklyn  and he finds one family member who's his  great grandson  ben greenbaum also played by seth rogen  so you have two seth rogens looking at  each other in this film so one of my  biggest problems with this film  is that i believe seth rogen is a great  straight man in any comedy film  but he is not a good funny man and i  feel like that was missing here because  herschel's supposed to be the funny man  that seth rogen is playing and honestly  i don't think seth rogen is interesting  enough or funny enough to play that part  it's not where he fits  he fits as a reactor and that's where  yeah he fits in the role of ben here  who's reacting to the crazy herschel and  you see this in all seth rogan's movies  his  moments shine when he's reacting to  anything ridiculous and he's playing  that straight man of correcting people  but when he tries to go in as the funny  guy himself  i don't feel it i don't think he's  interesting enough in that department  he's too normal in a sense and that  makes me feel like the character of  herschel suffers here  because i don't think seth rogen's the  right man for the part it reminded me of  the movie  elf with will ferrell now will ferrell  is the perfect funny man here  right he's never the straight man and if  you had someone like him playing a  herschel type role it works so  this movie felt like actually a really  just  dull boring version of the story of elf  where  a figure comes from almost like a  different time or land and is trying to  adjust and take in the big city  you've seen it a million times but  unlike elf it  leaves out the funny or fun part of it  the movie's in a very  grim color palette it's all blues and  greens here in gray  and it really fits the just feel of the  movie that it's dull and  that it never really escapes that and it  makes it really boring to watch  and it was one of those films i just  wanted to end  i thought it started okay and then 20  minutes in you're like this isn't good  and then 40 minutes in you're like how  has it only been 20 minutes  it just keeps drudging along for an hour  and a half run time which is  really just at this point unacceptable  with so many options to watch  you're going to see the reason that ben  is actually mad at herschel the main  reason  isn't that great in the sense of making  you as the audience  feel for ben a lot you kind of just like  eh and then that hurts the emotional  weight later on the emotional payoffs  it brings the stakes so low and if  you're gonna have low stakes and a  comedy that's fine but  you gotta make it funny then and it's  seth rogen doing those jokes he's in his  comfort zone with where  there's not much thought to it and it's  timely jokes but they're  really easy and anyone could have wrote  them kind of jokes referencing twitter  again referencing blogging  making stabs at hipster culture in  brooklyn because the character of ben  is based off a brooklyn hipster and the  story's  basically being told to have them both  learn from each other and him  embrace his jewish roots and then  herschel to pick up  the new values and him to kind of pick  up some of the old values  but just because you make that a good  theme  doesn't mean it pays off in the end and  because knowing it's based off a short  story  i feel like this story would really work  well as a short story  but it does not work as a film it's  paper thin here the plot it's  a classic story of him trying to get  revenge on this new being in his life  that's just a complete idiot and it  is just not funny enough to justify such  a thin plot  i also wish having a character like  herschel who  is a weird character he's off he's  supposed to be the funny one  that he had time to react to more actual  actors we know here where we only really  see him talk to  seth rogen as ben and background actors  so it's frustrating because i thought  maybe he'd  have more time with sarah snook or yorma  toconi but there  really isn't another player here for him  to work off of which i thought was a  very strange choice  i'm not like a seth rogen hater like i  think seth rogen's super talented  and i think he's one of the funniest  people listening to him on podcasts  interviews he's in talk shows i love him  as a person in that sense but  again you gotta be real too and realize  some actors are just great in certain  areas and others they're not really  meant for and i just don't  think it helped that he played the role  of herschel here as a funny man i just  don't think he is  and it's just falling on this crutch of  again  overdone so much but you have the one  dome character  and all you the humor is just the  reactions to him  like look he's an idiot again because he  did this and it gets old really quick  and you're going to see some critics  today say oh what a cute  timely story and the ending just meant  so much embracing his roots  and they're going to make us feel like  it's this great feel good story but it's  not  it's not earned enough it has that idea  it wants to do that but doesn't mean it  pulls it off and i don't think  it pulled it off in any way with the  theme i don't think it pulled off  the jokes i don't think the plot was  interesting and i just think it was a  bad movie and if even if you  think that maybe you liked how it ends  or had a really  good lesson here immoral and you felt  like it was earned  was it worth it in the entertainment  value was it worth it sitting there for  an hour and a half  not laughing and if you were laughing  more power to you but  i'd love to know because i didn't laugh  once in this film so so i would  totally avoid this film i'm giving this  one a 4.2  when you do see it let me know down  below what you thought of it and let me  know if you plan to watch it in general  please make sure to subscribe so you  don't miss one of my reviews i do tv  reviews as well i also do celebrity  interviews you don't miss any of those  and please follow me at stevewarly1 on  twitter instagram for more of me  and i'll see you next time

